From a461b47aed44b6f79fe805d0d06fd6e3ad64c910 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Miures Manager <contact@miures.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 18:37:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] The engine reads the sentence first (Intelligent Mode
 upgrade, Phase 3)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

interpretRequest in the engine turns a sentence into actions in the one
vocabulary (dry-run through applySurveyActions, so an edit that would be
refused comes back as a refusal with the engine's reason and a checked
fix), an answer from the survey's own graph (what depends on Q7, what
breaks if Q15 is deleted, untranslated questions, constructs, analyses),
a choice when a description fits several objects, or a hand-off to the
model only for what needs one (generation, rewording, translation text,
synthesis, findings). Ranges and relative targets ("skip Q8 through Q12",
"the next five questions"), options one at a time, randomization with
anchors, masks, compound requests, quota deletion. The condition
normaliser moves into the engine and learns "over / under / older than".

The Studio asks the engine first; its turns render on the copilot card
(internal engine · no model call) and join the same proposal, Changes
panel, Apply, undo and history; /api/ai/logic is called only without a
copilot, so a sentence costs at most one model call. diffSurveys now sees
option codes, flags, conditions, values, masks, custom code, validation
values and page breaks.

Engine 1607 tests; Phase 3 modules mutation-checked (99) and the follow-up
fixes (20); browser: engine-first (9), intelligent-mode adapted (55) and
the seven copilot suites pass.

