From d3cdc63c0c96214659d20b438f8433e4af6414c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Miures Manager <contact@miures.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:00:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] The review, what can be done to what is selected, and
 what it is wired to (Intelligent Mode upgrade, Phase 4)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Changes panel renders the engine's change tree: an Impact header,
survey and block changes, one card per question ("Q7 · Single choice ·
Do you own a car?") with a row per change — category, "Option 4 — United
States", old and new stacked and wrapping, what it affects, the
destructive note, its status. Every row and card can be unticked:
the actions behind it are left out (what else they made is said
first), Apply reads "Apply N of M changes" and applies only the included
actions, and History and the audit record say what was excluded. Options
preview their code, value, flags, condition, the question's order and
mask, and what reads them. The tab strip and everything in the panel wrap:
no sideways scrolling at 260, 360 or 520 px.

contextActions (engine) lists the operations valid for a question, an
option or a block, each a sentence the interpreter has already accepted,
or a template for the input box; dependencyReport (extracted from the
interpreter) draws what reads the object and what it reads, grouped,
every item navigating. Selecting a question with no proposal open shows
them. A condition the engine cannot read goes to the model with what was
detected (a near-miss or missing code is still refused with its fix), and
"Q3 is Yes or Maybe" is one question with two answers.

Engine 1613, Studio unit 234; 37 mutations (6 equivalent); browser
change-review (11) and all fifteen Intelligent-mode suites pass.

