 not (Intelligent Mode upgrade, Phase 5)

Every Intelligent Mode operation is a row of intelligent_operations
(migration 0047, applied to the project): prompt, source, interpreted
intent, detected objects, targets, proposed / applied / excluded /
refused changes, warnings, engine operations, model calls with their
cost, before and after, status. The server assigns the survey's AI change
number on apply (unique per survey, retried on a clash), so numbering
continues across sessions. /api/copilot/operations reads and writes it,
with an in-memory fallback until the table exists and in the sandbox.

Apply waits for the draft to save before saying so: SAVING, SAVED, NOT
SAVED with the reason and a retry, or SANDBOX (NOT SAVED); the record
follows. Grammar proposals are applied to a copy first, so a failed one
takes no undo step. Undo and redo are seen by the history. The History
tab shows each operation with its details, Compare, Restore and Reapply.

The auth-guard audit is clean again: the analysis-runs cron checks its
bearer token in each handler's first statement, and brand-scrape (which
writes nothing) is registered as needing no edit lock.

Studio unit 252; 22 mutations caught; browser history (8) and the
Intelligent-mode suites pass.

